# Public task inputs

The candidate receives the frozen API contract and UI contract in this directory. Evaluator-only
files remain outside `tasks/public/`.
# Lab Sample Pickup & Delivery — agent guidance

## Go file editing — read first, always

Before every `str_replace` on a `.go` file, run `file_editor view` on that file
and copy the exact bytes you see (including tabs, not spaces) as your `old_str`.
Never construct `old_str` from memory — indentation or whitespace mismatches cause
a silent no-op ("No replacement was performed") with no error, meaning the edit
never happens and the build still fails.

Pattern that works every time:
1. `file_editor view /workspace/backend/.../<file>.go` — read current content
2. Identify the exact lines to replace in the output
3. Use those exact bytes as `old_str` in `str_replace`

## Heredocs and shell scripts

Tab characters inside heredocs are mangled by the terminal. Do not use `python3 - <<'PY'`
or `cat <<'EOF'` to patch Go source. Instead write the script to a file first:

```
file_editor create /tmp/patch.py "<script content>"
python3 /tmp/patch.py
```

## Terminal output

Terminal observations (including `ls`) may contain ANSI escape sequences such as
`\x1b[?2004l` and `\x1b[?2004h` (bracketed paste mode). These are harmless noise —
ignore them. File content read via `file_editor view` is always clean.

## Context management

If you notice you are re-reading files you have already seen or re-planning work you
have already done, your context has likely been condensed. Re-read `AGENTS.md` and
your `app-setup/manifest.json` to reorient, then continue from the current build
state rather than starting over.

